# Shell scripts and rendered-template inputs MUST stay LF: a Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise corrupt shebangs and heredocs for
# the Git Bash-driven deploy/single pipeline (2026-09-03 Windows review).
# Everything text is LF: images.txt, env.example, compose.yaml, models.json and
# requirements.lock all checked out CRLF on the 2026-09-17 Windows run and the
# resolver refused images.txt ("expected 6 columns"). (web/ has its own file.)
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.tmpl text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
